  "scope": "Complete unchanged ThievableChestPlugin (its Chest enum and the anonymous pulse of searchTraps) and Pulse, compiled with Kotlin 1.8.20/JDK 11 against the pinned ConstLib 1.4.28 artifact. The Skills constants are pinned text spliced into an adapter shell; ContentAPI's animate and lock are adapters with the original bodies. Player (sendMessage with and without a delay, lock, animate, faceLocation), Skills (getLevel, getLifepoints, addExperience), the inventory (freeSlots, add for the player), the animator, ImpactHandler (manualHit, setDisabledTicks), Scenery (id, isActive, transform), SceneryBuilder.replace, SceneryDefinition's handlers and GameWorld (getTicks, the pulser) are recording adapters whose results come from declared case state; they are service inputs, not ports. The driver sets every constant's respawn tick back to 0 before a case (through setRespawn with a chosen tick), calls the registered plugin's handle with a scenery of the id a case names, and calls the submitted pulse's update itself; no pulse runner, option dispatch, live world, scenery replacement, hit, lock, inventory, ground item or experience behaviour is established by this corpus.",
